---
import { getImage } from "astro:assets";
import { S3Client, GetObjectCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-s3";
import { getSignedUrl } from "@aws-sdk/s3-request-presigner";
import { BandcampEmbed, MixcloudEmbed } from "@components/embedded-media";

const s3 = new S3Client({
	region: "auto",
	endpoint: import.meta.env.R2_ENDPOINT,
	credentials: {
		accessKeyId: import.meta.env.R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID,
		secretAccessKey: import.meta.env.R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,
	},
});

async function getMusicImage(key: string) {
	const signedUrl = await getSignedUrl(
		s3,
		new GetObjectCommand({
			Bucket: import.meta.env.R2_BUCKET,
			Key: key,
		}),
		{ expiresIn: 3600 },
	);
	return (
		await getImage({
			src: signedUrl,
			width: 1000,
			height: 1000,
			quality: "low",
			inferSize: true,
		})
	).src;
}

const elevatedSpiritImg = await getMusicImage(
	"music/matt f elevated spirit.jpg",
);
const contractsImg = await getMusicImage("music/prcsr contracts.jpg");
const asagayaImg = await getMusicImage("music/asagaya poster.jpg");
---

<div class="flex flex-col">
	<div class="flex flex-row-reverse gap-4 border-b-2 border-gray-800">
		<div class="w-1/2 overflow-hidden">
			<img
				src={elevatedSpiritImg}
				alt="Elevated Spirit by Matt F"
				class="w-full scale-105 grayscale transition-all duration-150 hover:scale-100 hover:grayscale-0"
			/>
		</div>
		<div class="flex w-1/2 flex-col gap-2">
			<p>
				This album is a collection of drum and bass music with an ambient style.
				I had some a capella samples I wanted to use for a song, as well as the
				desire to use the Apache instrumental break for the first time. These
				formed the basis of the track Black Cell. The sound of Cirrostratus was
				aiming to be a rolling drum and bass track. The long phasing pad is the
				primary element of this track and I built everything else around it. I
				also wanted to experiment with chopping different breaks in one track.
				This was the basis of the track Chopper. The track Information Overload
				was the result of listening to a lot of music on the label 720 Degrees
				at the time. Their style of drum and bass has a futuristic sound with
				heavy usage of E-mu Systems ROMpler synths. To achieve this sound I used
				a software version of the E-mu synths called Emulator III.
			</p>
			<BandcampEmbed
				albumId="3783468820"
				href="https://mattf.bandcamp.com/album/elevated-spirit"
				title="Elevated Spirit by Matt F"
			/>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="flex flex-row gap-4 border-b-2 border-gray-800">
		<div class="w-1/2 overflow-hidden">
			<img
				src={contractsImg}
				alt="Contracts by prcsr"
				class="w-full scale-105 grayscale transition-all duration-150 hover:scale-100 hover:grayscale-0"
			/>
		</div>
		<div class="flex w-1/2 flex-col gap-2">
			<p>
				The album Contracts was the result of a collaboration with the artist
				Wei. We aimed to establish a sinister, ambient soundscape influenced by
				Jesper Kyd. The primary synth I used for this was a Korg Triton -
				specifically its percussion and sound effect patches. There is a secret
				track at the end of the track Contracts.
			</p>
			<BandcampEmbed
				albumId="2620077534"
				href="https://dreamcatalogue.bandcamp.com/album/contracts"
				title="Contracts by prcsr"
			/>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="flex flex-row-reverse gap-4 border-b-2 border-gray-800">
		<div class="w-1/2 overflow-hidden">
			<img
				src={asagayaImg}
				alt="Asagaya Drift 20250905"
				class="w-full scale-105 grayscale transition-all duration-150 hover:scale-100 hover:grayscale-0"
			/>
		</div>
		<div class="flex w-1/2 flex-col gap-2">
			<p>
				This is a recording of a DJ set that occured in Asagaya around Autumn
				2025. I recorded it using a Sony WM-D6C onto RTM C90 Type I cassettes
				from the DJ deck RCA master output. That tape recorder comes with two
				settings for noise reduction but I left them disabled for the recording
				to get a vintage sound on the recording. The first hour of the audio is
				my own performance.
			</p>
			<MixcloudEmbed
				feed="%2FTotalMattF%2Fasagaya-drift-20250905%2F"
				title="Asagaya Drift 20250905"
			/>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
